  "contributors": "Christopher Daniel Pang supplied the PAL/RPL cut, the retained empty space and its return, and BLA accounting in the same units. Hearthline derived the prime-column allocation, its asymptotic refund, and the physical stock consequences in his program.",
  "formal_scope": "Greedy minimizes cumulative external draws among all legal plans and preserves the corresponding stock dominance. Both nested reversal identities and the lower bound at a cut are formal. The exact weighted Euclidean residue, its all-row bound and the quotient/lane record identity are formal.",
  "paper_scope": "All cutwise stock minima for an optimal pocket are attained simultaneously. The pocket cost at any uniform stock cap is G plus the sum of depth excesses. A proof using the row totals behind Granville and Soundararajan 1.5 forces K >= n*x*exp(c*sqrt(log M/log log M)) on each sufficiently late feasible board with an O(n^2) pocket, in each orientation. The common rounded columns recover an oscillating limiting fraction of primes and cost fewer than n*x extra lanes at every cut.",
  "review": {
    "type": "author self-review",
    "orientation": "Ordinary stock is limited after every physical distance. Releasing a column and filing jobs at that same distance can be performed together. The generous control checking only after prime arrivals is recorded separately.",
    "inventory": "Stock means actual still-eligible idle positions. The four-point reductions preserve final stock and add (depth-cap)_+ to spending. A separate dynamic search allowed deliberately paying early when finding the least draw on small fixtures.",
    "row_mean": "The asymptotic lower bound uses disjoint matrix rows and their mean, as proved on page 623 of the source. A single exceptional interval would not suffice with the prescribed total pocket. Positive parts control varying n-a even when some rows have the opposite sign.",
    "rounding": "For every retired row its last admissible source fixes the exact unused lanes. The map permits cross-prime use of an ordinary whole column while the global source sequence permits the inverse.",
    "range": "The strong all-head storage bound applies to the budgeted physical allocation model. It is not a general bound on algorithmic memory. The unknown all-head pocket fit remains open."
  },
